# HAYAT's thinking model: Qwythos-9B (Qwen 3.5, uncensored), tuned for accuracy
# and reproducibility. Built FROM the pulled GGUF so it inherits that model's
# Qwen 3.5 chat template, tool-calling format, vision projector and thinking
# support unchanged -- only the sampling is set here.
#
# Identity is NOT handled at this layer. The GGUF's chat template injects a
# "You are Qwythos, created by Empero AI" line, and that is dealt with the way
# every backend's self-description is: HAYAT's system preamble is authoritative
# and the leak guard corrects any residue in output. HAYAT is the agent, not
# the weights.
FROM hf.co/llmfan46/Qwythos-9B-Claude-Mythos-5-1M-uncensored-heretic-GGUF:Q4_K_M

# Qwen 3.5's own recommended sampling for factual, non-repetitive output.
# Temperature is deliberately omitted: the app sets it per role (0.1 reasoning,
# 0.3 conversation) and a PARAMETER here would only be a default it overrides.
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER min_p 0.0
# Qwen 3.5 degrades with a heavy repetition penalty; 1.05 is the documented
# ceiling that still discourages loops without clipping correct repetition.
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.05
PARAMETER repeat_last_n 64
# No fixed seed. A fixed seed made every identical question return a
# byte-identical answer, which read as HAYAT parroting itself the second time
# Mohsin asked -- "giving the same reply twice". Reproducibility is not worth
# sounding like a stuck record in conversation, so generation varies naturally.
# Stop tokens, so generation ends at the end of a turn rather than running on
# into a hallucinated next turn.
PARAMETER stop "<|im_end|>"
PARAMETER stop "<|endoftext|>"
